  "id": "3ceaac27-6a68-50db-b048-eb1a30aa6563",
  "slug": "caramel-corn-ii",
  "name": "Caramel Corn II",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "We always made this for Christmas. This recipe can also be made into 20 popcorn balls.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Add 1 tablespoon of the oil to a 4 quart saucepan, and heat over high heat. When oil is hot, add 1/2 cup of popping corn. Keep pan moving constantly. When corn stops popping, remove from heat. Repeat until all corn has been popped. Place popped corn into a buttered bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "In a 3 quart saucepan, combine sugar, salt, butter, dark corn syrup, and water. Stir until sugar dissolves. Stir in vinegar. Boil sugar mixture to hard ball stage, 248 degrees F (118 degrees C). Remove caramel from heat. Stir in soda. Beat to thoroughly dissolve the soda."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Pour hot caramel over popcorn, and quickly stir into popcorn; work quickly for the caramel sets up fast. Spread out on wax paper to cool. Store in a tightly covered container."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 10,
  "cooking_time_minutes": null,
  "preparation_time_minutes": null,
